---Profile for the container service agent pool.
---@class azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAgentPoolProfile
---@field eTag? string Unique read-only string used to implement optimistic concurrency. The eTag value will change when the resource is updated. Specify an if-match or if-none-match header with the eTag value for a subsequent request to enable optimistic concurrency per the normal eTag convention.
---@field count? number Number of agents (VMs) to host docker containers. Allowed values must be in the range of 0 to 1000 (inclusive) for user pools and in the range of 1 to 1000 (inclusive) for system pools. The default value is 1.
---@field vmSize? string The size of the agent pool VMs. VM size availability varies by region. If a node contains insufficient compute resources (memory, cpu, etc) pods might fail to run correctly. For more details on restricted VM sizes, see: https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/quotas-skus-regions
---@field osDiskSizeGB? number OS Disk Size in GB to be used to specify the disk size for every machine in the master/agent pool. If you specify 0, it will apply the default osDisk size according to the vmSize specified.
---@field osDiskType? azure.containerservice.OSDiskType The OS disk type to be used for machines in the agent pool. The default is 'Ephemeral' if the VM supports it and has a cache disk larger than the requested OSDiskSizeGB. Otherwise, defaults to 'Managed'. May not be changed after creation. For more information see [Ephemeral OS](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/cluster-configuration#ephemeral-os).
---@field kubeletDiskType? azure.containerservice.KubeletDiskType Determines the placement of emptyDir volumes, container runtime data root, and Kubelet ephemeral storage.
---@field workloadRuntime? azure.containerservice.WorkloadRuntime Determines the type of workload a node can run.
---@field messageOfTheDay? string Message of the day for Linux nodes, base64-encoded. A base64-encoded string which will be written to /etc/motd after decoding. This allows customization of the message of the day for Linux nodes. It must not be specified for Windows nodes. It must be a static string (i.e., will be printed raw and not be executed as a script).
---@field vnetSubnetID? string The ID of the subnet which agent pool nodes and optionally pods will join on startup. If this is not specified, a VNET and subnet will be generated and used. If no podSubnetID is specified, this applies to nodes and pods, otherwise it applies to just nodes. This is of the form: /subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/{virtualNetworkName}/subnets/{subnetName}
---@field podSubnetID? string The ID of the subnet which pods will join when launched. If omitted, pod IPs are statically assigned on the node subnet (see vnetSubnetID for more details). This is of the form: /subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/{virtualNetworkName}/subnets/{subnetName}
---@field podIPAllocationMode? azure.containerservice.PodIPAllocationMode Pod IP Allocation Mode. The IP allocation mode for pods in the agent pool. Must be used with podSubnetId. The default is 'DynamicIndividual'.
---@field maxPods? number The maximum number of pods that can run on a node.
---@field osType? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAgentPoolProfileOsType The operating system type. The default is Linux.
---@field osSKU? azure.containerservice.OSSKU Specifies the OS SKU used by the agent pool. The default is Ubuntu if OSType is Linux. The default is Windows2019 when Kubernetes <= 1.24 or Windows2022 when Kubernetes >= 1.25 if OSType is Windows.
---@field maxCount? number The maximum number of nodes for auto-scaling
---@field minCount? number The minimum number of nodes for auto-scaling
---@field enableAutoScaling? boolean Whether to enable auto-scaler
---@field scaleDownMode? azure.containerservice.ScaleDownMode The scale down mode to use when scaling the Agent Pool. This also effects the cluster autoscaler behavior. If not specified, it defaults to Delete.
---@field type? azure.containerservice.AgentPoolType The type of Agent Pool.
---@field mode? azure.containerservice.AgentPoolMode The mode of an agent pool. A cluster must have at least one 'System' Agent Pool at all times. For additional information on agent pool restrictions and best practices, see: https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/use-system-pools
---@field orchestratorVersion? string The version of Kubernetes specified by the user. Both patch version <major.minor.patch> (e.g. 1.20.13) and <major.minor> (e.g. 1.20) are supported. When <major.minor> is specified, the latest supported GA patch version is chosen automatically. Updating the cluster with the same <major.minor> once it has been created (e.g. 1.14.x -> 1.14) will not trigger an upgrade, even if a newer patch version is available. As a best practice, you should upgrade all node pools in an AKS cluster to the same Kubernetes version. The node pool version must have the same major version as the control plane. The node pool minor version must be within two minor versions of the control plane version. The node pool version cannot be greater than the control plane version. For more information see [upgrading a node pool](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/use-multiple-node-pools#upgrade-a-node-pool).
---@field currentOrchestratorVersion? string The version of Kubernetes the Agent Pool is running. If orchestratorVersion is a fully specified version <major.minor.patch>, this field will be exactly equal to it. If orchestratorVersion is <major.minor>, this field will contain the full <major.minor.patch> version being used.
---@field nodeImageVersion? string The version of the node image. Setting this value triggers an agentPool rollback. Only values from `recentlyUsedVersions` are allowed.
---@field upgradeSettings? azure.containerservice.AgentPoolUpgradeSettings Settings for upgrading the agentpool
---@field provisioningState? string The current deployment or provisioning state.
---@field powerState? azure.containerservice.PowerState Whether the Agent Pool is running or stopped. When an Agent Pool is first created it is initially Running. The Agent Pool can be stopped by setting this field to Stopped. A stopped Agent Pool stops all of its VMs and does not accrue billing charges. An Agent Pool can only be stopped if it is Running and provisioning state is Succeeded
---@field availabilityZones? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAgentPoolProfileAvailabilityZonesList The list of Availability zones to use for nodes. This can only be specified if the AgentPoolType property is 'VirtualMachineScaleSets'.
---@field enableNodePublicIP? boolean Whether each node is allocated its own public IP. Some scenarios may require nodes in a node pool to receive their own dedicated public IP addresses. A common scenario is for gaming workloads, where a console needs to make a direct connection to a cloud virtual machine to minimize hops. For more information see [assigning a public IP per node](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/use-multiple-node-pools#assign-a-public-ip-per-node-for-your-node-pools). The default is false.
---@field nodePublicIPPrefixID? string The public IP prefix ID which VM nodes should use IPs from. This is of the form: /subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Network/publicIPPrefixes/{publicIPPrefixName}
---@field scaleSetPriority? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAgentPoolProfileScaleSetPriority The Virtual Machine Scale Set priority.
---@field scaleSetEvictionPolicy? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAgentPoolProfileScaleSetEvictionPolicy The Virtual Machine Scale Set eviction policy. The eviction policy specifies what to do with the VM when it is evicted. The default is Delete. For more information about eviction see [spot VMs](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/virtual-machines/spot-vms)
---@field spotMaxPrice? number The max price (in US Dollars) you are willing to pay for spot instances. Possible values are any decimal value greater than zero or -1 which indicates default price to be up-to on-demand. Possible values are any decimal value greater than zero or -1 which indicates the willingness to pay any on-demand price. For more details on spot pricing, see [spot VMs pricing](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/virtual-machines/spot-vms#pricing)
---@field tags? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAgentPoolProfileTagsMap The tags to be persisted on the agent pool virtual machine scale set.
---@field nodeLabels? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAgentPoolProfileNodeLabelsMap The node labels to be persisted across all nodes in agent pool.
---@field nodeTaints? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAgentPoolProfileNodeTaintsList The taints added to new nodes during node pool create and scale. For example, key=value:NoSchedule.
---@field proximityPlacementGroupID? string The ID for Proximity Placement Group.
---@field kubeletConfig? azure.containerservice.KubeletConfig The Kubelet configuration on the agent pool nodes.
---@field linuxOSConfig? azure.containerservice.LinuxOSConfig The OS configuration of Linux agent nodes.
---@field enableEncryptionAtHost? boolean Whether to enable host based OS and data drive encryption. This is only supported on certain VM sizes and in certain Azure regions. For more information, see: https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/enable-host-encryption
---@field enableUltraSSD? boolean Whether to enable UltraSSD
---@field enableFIPS? boolean Whether to use a FIPS-enabled OS. See [Add a FIPS-enabled node pool](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/use-multiple-node-pools#add-a-fips-enabled-node-pool-preview) for more details.
---@field gpuInstanceProfile? azure.containerservice.GPUInstanceProfile GPUInstanceProfile to be used to specify GPU MIG instance profile for supported GPU VM SKU.
---@field creationData? azure.containerservice.CreationData CreationData to be used to specify the source Snapshot ID if the node pool will be created/upgraded using a snapshot.
---@field capacityReservationGroupID? string The fully qualified resource ID of the Capacity Reservation Group to provide virtual machines from a reserved group of Virtual Machines. This is of the form: '/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourcegroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Compute/capacityreservationgroups/{capacityReservationGroupName}' Customers use it to create an agentpool with a specified CRG. For more information see [Capacity Reservation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/virtual-machines/capacity-reservation-overview)
---@field hostGroupID? string The fully qualified resource ID of the Dedicated Host Group to provision virtual machines from, used only in creation scenario and not allowed to changed once set. This is of the form: /subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Compute/hostGroups/{hostGroupName}. For more information see [Azure dedicated hosts](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/virtual-machines/dedicated-hosts).
