---Properties of the managed cluster.
---@class azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterProperties
---@field provisioningState? string The current provisioning state.
---@field powerState? azure.containerservice.PowerState The Power State of the cluster.
---@field maxAgentPools? number The max number of agent pools for the managed cluster.
---@field kubernetesVersion? string The version of Kubernetes specified by the user. Both patch version <major.minor.patch> (e.g. 1.20.13) and <major.minor> (e.g. 1.20) are supported. When <major.minor> is specified, the latest supported GA patch version is chosen automatically. Updating the cluster with the same <major.minor> once it has been created (e.g. 1.14.x -> 1.14) will not trigger an upgrade, even if a newer patch version is available. When you upgrade a supported AKS cluster, Kubernetes minor versions cannot be skipped. All upgrades must be performed sequentially by major version number. For example, upgrades between 1.14.x -> 1.15.x or 1.15.x -> 1.16.x are allowed, however 1.14.x -> 1.16.x is not allowed. See [upgrading an AKS cluster](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/upgrade-cluster) for more details.
---@field currentKubernetesVersion? string The version of Kubernetes the Managed Cluster is running. If kubernetesVersion was a fully specified version <major.minor.patch>, this field will be exactly equal to it. If kubernetesVersion was <major.minor>, this field will contain the full <major.minor.patch> version being used.
---@field dnsPrefix? string The DNS prefix of the Managed Cluster. This cannot be updated once the Managed Cluster has been created.
---@field fqdnSubdomain? string The FQDN subdomain of the private cluster with custom private dns zone. This cannot be updated once the Managed Cluster has been created.
---@field fqdn? string The FQDN of the master pool.
---@field privateFQDN? string The FQDN of private cluster.
---@field azurePortalFQDN? string The special FQDN used by the Azure Portal to access the Managed Cluster. This FQDN is for use only by the Azure Portal and should not be used by other clients. The Azure Portal requires certain Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) headers to be sent in some responses, which Kubernetes APIServer doesn't handle by default. This special FQDN supports CORS, allowing the Azure Portal to function properly.
---@field agentPoolProfiles? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterPropertiesAgentPoolProfilesList The agent pool properties.
---@field linuxProfile? azure.containerservice.ContainerServiceLinuxProfile The profile for Linux VMs in the Managed Cluster.
---@field windowsProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterWindowsProfile The profile for Windows VMs in the Managed Cluster.
---@field servicePrincipalProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterServicePrincipalProfile Information about a service principal identity for the cluster to use for manipulating Azure APIs.
---@field addonProfiles? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterPropertiesAddonProfilesMap The profile of managed cluster add-on.
---@field podIdentityProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterPodIdentityProfile The pod identity profile of the Managed Cluster. See [use AAD pod identity](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/use-azure-ad-pod-identity) for more details on AAD pod identity integration.
---@field oidcIssuerProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterOIDCIssuerProfile The OIDC issuer profile of the Managed Cluster.
---@field nodeResourceGroup? string The name of the resource group containing agent pool nodes.
---@field nodeResourceGroupProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterNodeResourceGroupProfile Profile of the node resource group configuration.
---@field enableRBAC? boolean Whether to enable Kubernetes Role-Based Access Control.
---@field supportPlan? azure.containerservice.KubernetesSupportPlan The support plan for the Managed Cluster. If unspecified, the default is 'KubernetesOfficial'.
---@field enableFIPS? boolean Whether to enable FIPS mode at the cluster level. When enabled, this setting enforces FIPS compliance for all AKS-managed components, such as the node operating system, addons, and [managed containerized components](https://aka.ms/aks/components/docs). See [Enable cluster-wide FIPS](https://aka.ms/aks/fips) for more details. When this property is enabled, all node pools in the cluster must also be FIPS-enabled. Although this property is available in a stable API version, cluster-wide FIPS remains a preview feature. Write requests whose resulting cluster state has this property set to true require the `Microsoft.ContainerService/EnableFIPSPreview` subscription feature registration.
---@field networkProfile? azure.containerservice.ContainerServiceNetworkProfile The network configuration profile.
---@field aadProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAADProfile The Azure Active Directory configuration.
---@field autoUpgradeProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAutoUpgradeProfile The auto upgrade configuration.
---@field upgradeSettings? azure.containerservice.ClusterUpgradeSettings Settings for upgrading a cluster.
---@field autoScalerProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterPropertiesAutoScalerProfile Parameters to be applied to the cluster-autoscaler when enabled
---@field apiServerAccessProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAPIServerAccessProfile The access profile for managed cluster API server.
---@field diskEncryptionSetID? string The Resource ID of the disk encryption set to use for enabling encryption at rest. This is of the form: '/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.Compute/diskEncryptionSets/{encryptionSetName}'
---@field identityProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterPropertiesIdentityProfileMap The user identity associated with the managed cluster. This identity will be used by the kubelet. Only one user assigned identity is allowed. The only accepted key is "kubeletidentity", with value of "resourceId": "/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities/{identityName}".
---@field privateLinkResources? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterPropertiesPrivateLinkResourcesList Private link resources associated with the cluster.
---@field disableLocalAccounts? boolean If local accounts should be disabled on the Managed Cluster. If set to true, getting static credentials will be disabled for this cluster. This must only be used on Managed Clusters that are AAD enabled. For more details see [disable local accounts](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/aks/managed-aad#disable-local-accounts-preview).
---@field httpProxyConfig? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterHTTPProxyConfig Configurations for provisioning the cluster with HTTP proxy servers.
---@field securityProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterSecurityProfile Security profile for the managed cluster.
---@field storageProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterStorageProfile Storage profile for the managed cluster.
---@field ingressProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterIngressProfile Ingress profile for the managed cluster.
---@field publicNetworkAccess? azure.containerservice.PublicNetworkAccess PublicNetworkAccess of the managedCluster. Allow or deny public network access for AKS
---@field workloadAutoScalerProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterWorkloadAutoScalerProfile Workload Auto-scaler profile for the managed cluster.
---@field azureMonitorProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAzureMonitorProfile Azure Monitor addon profiles for monitoring the managed cluster.
---@field serviceMeshProfile? azure.containerservice.ServiceMeshProfile Service mesh profile for a managed cluster.
---@field resourceUID? string The resourceUID uniquely identifies ManagedClusters that reuse ARM ResourceIds (i.e: create, delete, create sequence)
---@field metricsProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterMetricsProfile Optional cluster metrics configuration.
---@field nodeProvisioningProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterNodeProvisioningProfile Node provisioning settings that apply to the whole cluster.
---@field bootstrapProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterBootstrapProfile Profile of the cluster bootstrap configuration.
---@field aiToolchainOperatorProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterAIToolchainOperatorProfile AI toolchain operator settings that apply to the whole cluster.
---@field schedulerProfile? azure.containerservice.SchedulerProfile Profile with scheduler-related settings, like the configuration mode for each scheduler managed by AKS. See https://aka.ms/aks/scheduler-profile.
---@field hostedSystemProfile? azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterHostedSystemProfile Settings for hosted system addons. For more information, see https://aka.ms/aks/automatic/systemcomponents.
