---Parameters to be applied to the cluster-autoscaler when enabled
---@class azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterPropertiesAutoScalerProfile
---@field balance_similar_node_groups? string Detects similar node pools and balances the number of nodes between them. Valid values are 'true' and 'false'
---@field daemonset_eviction_for_empty_nodes? boolean DaemonSet pods will be gracefully terminated from empty nodes. If set to true, all daemonset pods on empty nodes will be evicted before deletion of the node. If the daemonset pod cannot be evicted another node will be chosen for scaling. If set to false, the node will be deleted without ensuring that daemonset pods are deleted or evicted.
---@field daemonset_eviction_for_occupied_nodes? boolean DaemonSet pods will be gracefully terminated from non-empty nodes. If set to true, all daemonset pods on occupied nodes will be evicted before deletion of the node. If the daemonset pod cannot be evicted another node will be chosen for scaling. If set to false, the node will be deleted without ensuring that daemonset pods are deleted or evicted.
---@field ignore_daemonsets_utilization? boolean Should CA ignore DaemonSet pods when calculating resource utilization for scaling down. If set to true, the resources used by daemonset will be taken into account when making scaling down decisions.
---@field expander? azure.containerservice.Expander|string The expander to use when scaling up. If not specified, the default is 'random'. See [expanders](https://github.com/kubernetes/autoscaler/blob/master/cluster-autoscaler/FAQ.md#what-are-expanders) for more information.
---@field max_empty_bulk_delete? string The maximum number of empty nodes that can be deleted at the same time. This must be a positive integer. The default is 10.
---@field max_graceful_termination_sec? string The maximum number of seconds the cluster autoscaler waits for pod termination when trying to scale down a node. The default is 600.
---@field max_node_provision_time? string The maximum time the autoscaler waits for a node to be provisioned. The default is '15m'. Values must be an integer followed by an 'm'. No unit of time other than minutes (m) is supported.
---@field max_total_unready_percentage? string The maximum percentage of unready nodes in the cluster. After this percentage is exceeded, cluster autoscaler halts operations. The default is 45. The maximum is 100 and the minimum is 0.
---@field new_pod_scale_up_delay? string Ignore unscheduled pods before they're a certain age. For scenarios like burst/batch scale where you don't want CA to act before the kubernetes scheduler could schedule all the pods, you can tell CA to ignore unscheduled pods before they're a certain age. The default is '0s'. Values must be an integer followed by a unit ('s' for seconds, 'm' for minutes, 'h' for hours, etc).
---@field ok_total_unready_count? string The number of allowed unready nodes, irrespective of max-total-unready-percentage. This must be an integer. The default is 3.
---@field scan_interval? string How often cluster is reevaluated for scale up or down. The default is '10'. Values must be an integer number of seconds.
---@field scale_down_delay_after_add? string How long after scale up that scale down evaluation resumes. The default is '10m'. Values must be an integer followed by an 'm'. No unit of time other than minutes (m) is supported.
---@field scale_down_delay_after_delete? string How long after node deletion that scale down evaluation resumes. The default is the scan-interval. Values must be an integer followed by an 'm'. No unit of time other than minutes (m) is supported.
---@field scale_down_delay_after_failure? string How long after scale down failure that scale down evaluation resumes. The default is '3m'. Values must be an integer followed by an 'm'. No unit of time other than minutes (m) is supported.
---@field scale_down_unneeded_time? string How long a node should be unneeded before it is eligible for scale down. The default is '10m'. Values must be an integer followed by an 'm'. No unit of time other than minutes (m) is supported.
---@field scale_down_unready_time? string How long an unready node should be unneeded before it is eligible for scale down. The default is '20m'. Values must be an integer followed by an 'm'. No unit of time other than minutes (m) is supported.
---@field scale_down_utilization_threshold? string Node utilization level, defined as sum of requested resources divided by capacity, below which a node can be considered for scale down. The default is '0.5'.
---@field skip_nodes_with_local_storage? string If cluster autoscaler will skip deleting nodes with pods with local storage, for example, EmptyDir or HostPath. The default is true.
---@field skip_nodes_with_system_pods? string If cluster autoscaler will skip deleting nodes with pods from kube-system (except for DaemonSet or mirror pods). The default is true.

---The user identity associated with the managed cluster. This identity will be used by the kubelet. Only one user assigned identity is allowed. The only accepted key is "kubeletidentity", with value of "resourceId": "/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/resourceGroups/{resourceGroupName}/providers/Microsoft.ManagedIdentity/userAssignedIdentities/{identityName}".
---@alias azure.containerservice.ManagedClusterPropertiesIdentityProfileMap { [string]: azure.containerservice.UserAssignedIdentity }

