---@field name string Name is the name of the property; it should be a Kubernetes label name.
---@field operator azure.containerservice.PlacementV1PropertySelectorOperator|string Operator specifies the relationship between a cluster's observed value of the specified property and the values given in the requirement.
---@field values azure.containerservice.PlacementV1PropertySelectorRequirementValuesList Values are a list of values of the specified property which Fleet will compare against the observed values of individual member clusters in accordance with the given operator. At this moment, each value should be a Kubernetes quantity. For more information, see https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource#Quantity. If the operator is Gt (greater than), Ge (greater than or equal to), Lt (less than), or `Le` (less than or equal to), Eq (equal to), or Ne (ne), exactly one value must be specified in the list.

---Values are a list of values of the specified property which Fleet will compare against the observed values of individual member clusters in accordance with the given operator. At this moment, each value should be a Kubernetes quantity. For more information, see https://pkg.go.dev/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource#Quantity. If the operator is Gt (greater than), Ge (greater than or equal to), Lt (less than), or `Le` (less than or equal to), Eq (equal to), or Ne (ne), exactly one value must be specified in the list.
---@alias azure.containerservice.PlacementV1PropertySelectorRequirementValuesList string[]

---Toleration allows ClusterResourcePlacement to tolerate any taint that matches the triple <key,value,effect> using the matching operator <operator>.
---@class azure.containerservice.PlacementV1Toleration
---@field key? string Key is the taint key that the toleration applies to. Empty means match all taint keys. If the key is empty, operator must be Exists; this combination means to match all values and all keys.
---@field operator? azure.containerservice.CoreV1TolerationOperator|string Operator represents a key's relationship to the value. Valid operators are Exists and Equal. Defaults to Equal. Exists is equivalent to wildcard for value, so that a ClusterResourcePlacement can tolerate all taints of a particular category.
---@field value? string Value is the taint value the toleration matches to. If the operator is Exists, the value should be empty, otherwise just a regular string.
---@field effect? azure.containerservice.CoreV1TaintEffect|string Effect indicates the taint effect to match. Empty means match all taint effects. When specified, only allowed value is NoSchedule.

